#: ../../source/fun_project/08-fun-Touch_toggle_light.rst:70
msgid "setup() function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/08-fun-Touch_toggle_light.rst:84
msgid "This function runs once when the Arduino is powered on or reset. Here, the touch sensor is set as an input (it will read values), while the LEDs are set as outputs (we will set their values). Also, the serial communication is started to allow debugging, and the initial touch state is read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/08-fun-Touch_toggle_light.rst:86
msgid "loop() function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/08-fun-Touch_toggle_light.rst:114
msgid "In the main loop, the current touch state is read and compared with the previous one. If a touch is detected (transition from LOW to HIGH), all LEDs are turned off, and the next one in the sequence is turned on."
msgstr ""

